Playwright CLI commands
--------------------------

To run the tests -> npx playwright test
To run the tests with browser open -> npx playwright test --headed
To run tests under specific project -> npx playwright test --project=chromium --headed
To run a specific test/spec file -> npx playwright test spec example.spec.ts --project=chromium --headed
To run by test name -> npx playwright test -g "has title" --project=chromium --headed
To open the results of last execution -> npx playwright show-report --> http://localhost:9323/


Annotations to be used inside test file
----------------------------------------
test.only -> to run only that test
test.skip -> to skip that test


Test Execution
----------------------------------
To run tests in UI mode -> npx playwright test --ui
To enble the trace option -> npx playwright test --project=chromium --trace on
To debug tests locally --> npx playwright test --project=chromium --debug


What is promise?
----------------------------------
Promise is a type of function in JavaScript that waits for the desired or expected condition to be executed.
Promise can be resolved or rejected.
And if the expected condition is satisfied within the timeout, it is resolved.
if the condition is NOT satisfied, promise is rejected and the step is failed.
<<<playwright.dev/docs/actionability>>> Auto waiting where we have table with all action methods and for which these action methods are waiting for
default wait time is 30seconds for the element to be visible.


